## Why its actually better
In C++, **vector::swap** swaps internal pointers rather than copying elements one by one.
In this code first loop takes O(N) time because it swaps row pointers.The standard approach takes O(N^2) time to reverse elements inside every row.
This approach performs fewer total element-by-element swaps, making it slightly faster in practice for standard C++ vectors.

